Patch for miic, branch causalccc, commit 5ca0b22 (notebook 10, change 2).
The confidence cut computes the MI of every edge on 100 shuffled datasets. Since each shuffled term exp(-I'_shuffle)
is in ]0, 1], bounds on their mean settle the cut decision early, often after one shuffle (or none when
I' < ln(1 / conf_threshold)); the remaining shuffles of a decided edge are not computed. Decisions are unchanged; the
exported confidence of an edge decided early is a bound. Shuffles are still drawn, so the random stream is unchanged.
Apply with: patch -p1 -d <miic source> < 02_confidence_early_decision.patch (see scripts/benchmarks/build_miic_variant.sh)

